Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Scope the shared radial scale to Figure 1

The previous commit pinned axis limits on every 3D panel, which shrank the
edema signal in Figure 3 relative to the healthy signal in Figure 2 and made
a flat reconstruction small in Figures 4 and 5. Only Figure 1 wants that.

Figure 1 keeps it: that panel exists to show the edema response is genuinely
smaller than the healthy one, so size has to carry meaning there.

Figures 2 and 3 are back to how they were and are again on the same footing
as each other -- they are about the SHAPE of the signal at each shell and
SNR, and one of them rendered small buys nothing. Figures 4 and 5 likewise
revert to unscaled glyphs with autoscaled panels; the fmax computed across
both of them is removed rather than left unused.

GLYPH_LIM's comment now says it is Figure 1 only, and why, so the scoping is
not mistaken later for an oversight.

No simulation was run. The figure block was re-executed against the graphics
stubs.

