Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Update the handoff for the manuscript simulation

Records what the next agent needs and cannot reconstruct from the diff.

Section 1 gains the notebooks: what each is for, that every knob is in one
Configuration block, that notebooks/README.md lists what each CHECK
establishes, and that the manuscript file is 42 SMI.fit calls at its
defaults with NREP as the knob.

Section 3 gains the shared-scale trap, which cost a review cycle: axis equal
fixes a panel's aspect RATIO, not its LIMITS, so scaling a glyph's radius is
invisible unless the panel is pinned too. With the corollary -- only use a
shared scale where size is the point, which here is Figure 1 alone.

Section 4 gains two real-data traps that synthetic protocols never show. A
.bvec is unit only to ~1e-6 at seven significant figures, which degrades the
Lmax 8 zonal identity from 1e-15 to 5e-7 for anything reading g(3) as
cos(theta). A .bval records EFFECTIVE b, so "b = 0" is 5 s/mm^2 and the
shells jitter across 18 distinct values.

Section 6.5 is new: what the manuscript simulation is set up to measure, and
the resolvability table that justifies using 60 degrees alone -- 30 never
separates at kappa = 16 and needs kappa >= 48, 45 only from Lmax 6 up. Notes
the consequence for run_smi_batch_mod.m, which runs max(Lmax) = 4 on real
subjects and therefore cannot resolve 45 degrees at any SNR. Both kernels
are tabulated with the reasoning behind the two deliberate departures in the
edema one, and the section states the framing to use: edema has LESS
ANISOTROPIC SIGNAL amplified in inverse proportion by dividing by K_l, not
"more noise" -- the noise is identical.

Section 8 is reordered around what is actually next: run the manuscript
simulation at full size, wire up the CSD arms through the hook that is
already in place, revisit the regularization sweep the user deferred to its
own patch, and regenerate the Reports tables on the real protocol. It also
records that NO figure in any notebook has ever been verified to render,
since Octave's print is broken here, and that this gap already shipped one
real bug.

The edema scope marker in the old section 8 is removed: it is done.

